<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Drunken Sailor Medley (John Baltzell)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">c. 1923</span><span class="sg-chain-h">fiddle reel</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Scotch Strathspey and Reel (Percy Grainger)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1924</span><span class="sg-chain-h">worked into</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Three Shanties for Woodwind Quintet, Op. 4 (Malcolm Arnold)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1943</span><span class="sg-chain-h">melody used</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">We Have a King Who Rides a Donkey (Fred Kaan)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">hymn to the same tune</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Caligari's Mirror (Pere Ubu)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1978</span><span class="sg-chain-h">post-punk reworking</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Gina, Dale Haze and the Champions</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1981</span><span class="sg-chain-h">disco version, an Irish top 20 hit</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Up as She Rises (Sam Spence, NFL Films)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">melody used</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Truman Show (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1998</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Fisherman's Friends (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2019</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Óró sé do bheatha abhaile</span><span class="sg-chain-h">an Irish song it resembles (chord progression, repeated words over melodic sequences)</span></li></ul></section>
